# Crop Disease Detection - Dataset Exploration

**Group problem area:** We imagine an application that lets a farmer take a photo of a crop leaf and immediately see an instant disease diagnosis thanks to an ML image classification engine.

**Dataset explored:** We have looked at the PlantVillage Dataset, from Hughes and Salathé 2015 which is kept at github.com/spMohanty/PlantVillage-Dataset.
## 1. Candidate open source datasets

The table below lists the open source datasets considered for this problem area, along with the variable in each that would serve as the **expected output (target label)** of the final application.

| # | Dataset | Description | Expected output variable |
|---|---------|-------------|---------------------------|
| 1 | **PlantVillage** (spMohanty/PlantVillage-Dataset) | 54,305 leaf images taken in lab conditions, 14 crop species, 38 crop-disease classes | `disease_label` — the crop-disease (or class) of the leaf |
| 2 | **New Plant Diseases Dataset** (Kaggle augmented version of PlantVillage) | Offline-augmented version of PlantVillage, around 87,000 images, same 38 classes | `disease_label` — crop-disease class |
| 3 | **PlantDoc** (Singh et al. 2020) | Around 2,598 real-world field images (not taken in lab backgrounds), 13 species, 27 classes | `disease_label` — crop-disease class, under real field conditions |
| 4 | **Cassava Leaf Disease Classification** (Kaggle / Makerere AI Lab) | Field images of cassava leaves collected in Uganda, around 21,397 images, 5 classes (4 diseases plus healthy) | `disease_class` — cassava disease category |

### Why PlantVillage was selected
- It is the largest and most balanced in terms of classes among the candidates with 54,305 labeled images spread across 38 classes.
- It is the commonly used dataset, in plant disease classification research, which helps in checking how well our model works compared to results that have already been published.
- The dataset was originally curated specifically to support the development of **mobile** disease diagnostic tools using machine learning  a direct match for our project's ML + Mobile App approach.

