## 3. Building the working dataframe

Since this is an image dataset "rows" and "columns" refer to a metadata table we construct. Each row represents one image and the columns provide details about that image. These details include the file path, the crop species, the disease label, the health status, the file format and the size. We organize the information this way so each image has its row with all relevant data, in the correct columns. This metadata table is what the exploration questions below are answered against.
import os
import pandas as pd

DATA_DIR = "PlantVillage-Dataset/raw/color"

records = []
for class_folder in os.listdir(DATA_DIR):
    class_path = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, class_folder)
    if not os.path.isdir(class_path):
        continue
    if "___" in class_folder:
        crop, disease = class_folder.split("___", 1)
    else:
        crop, disease = class_folder, "unknown"
    for filename in os.listdir(class_path):
        filepath = os.path.join(class_path, filename)
        records.append({
            "filepath": filepath,
            "crop_species": crop,
            "disease_label": disease,
            "is_healthy": disease.lower() == "healthy",
            "file_extension": filename.split(".")[-1].lower(),
            "file_size_kb": round(os.path.getsize(filepath) / 1024, 2)
        })

df = pd.DataFrame(records)
df.head()
